Subject: [PATCH] pandora: define IOAcceleratorES's meta class, the one line 0333 was carrying

0184 declares the class with OSDeclareDefaultStructors only, which declares the
meta class but never defines it.  The definition lived in 0333, together with a
registry sampler (a publishing thread that registers synchronously after 1.5 s
and then queries the service plane every 2 s between 44 s and 56 s).

k354 dropped 0333 and the kernel stopped linking:

  "IOAcceleratorES::gMetaClass", referenced from:
      AGXAccelerator::MetaClass::MetaClass() in PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpo
  "IOAcceleratorES::IOAcceleratorES(OSMetaClass const*)", referenced from: ...

So keep the definition and leave the sampler out: with the class defined by one
line, AGXAccelerator is the same 0184 personality that reached the lock screen in
log53/log56, and 0340's guard change is the only behavioural difference.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/PandoraAdrenoGpu.cpp
@@ -597,6 +597,12 @@
 class IOAcceleratorES : public IOService {
 	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(IOAcceleratorES);
 };
 
+/*
+ * 0343: OSDeclareDefaultStructors leaves gMetaClass undefined, so AGXAccelerator cannot link
+ * without this.  0333 used to carry the line, along with a registry sampler that is not wanted
+ * here: the node published by 0184 is the one backboardd already matches and opens.
+ */
+OSDefineMetaClassAndStructors(IOAcceleratorES, IOService);
+
 class AGXAccelerator : public IOAcceleratorES {
 	OSDeclareDefaultStructors(AGXAccelerator);
